# integration.suite — the full-integration flows that run in throwaway
# containers: every node in its own Docker container on one network.
#
# Run it with `--docker` on a host with a Docker engine; without --docker it
# runs in local worlds. Every test here is Docker-eligible: no VM ops, and
# nothing local_only; a listener the test serves is bound at the node's
# host_ip (host_listener). The planner refuses a test that is not.
#
# The order is a preference among siblings; the planner computes the run
# order from each test's `after`. expel-node is listed before hold-purge so
# that hold-purge, which also ends a world, forks instead of expel-node.
smoke
claim-window
token-less-setup
signer-app
admission-policies
bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node
blueprints-two-node
apphost-origin
sign-contract-guard
request-grant-scope
swarm-authz-matrix
services-swarm
object-store
object-store-peer
read-remote-peer
read-swarm
expel-node
hold-purge
hold-isolation
swarm-roster-sync
expel-propagation
import-user-software-key
introduce-node-setup
introduce-node
manager-setup
policy-delegate
indexer-cursor
swarm-member-restart
expel-survives-restart
